# Threadline Operator Hiring Scorecard

## Hire trigger
Only hire once the Delivery Load Ledger shows repetitive coordination/research/admin work is a real capacity constraint and the founder has personally proven the workflow.

## Traits
- High conscientiousness / follow-through.
- Strong written judgement.
- Evidence discipline; never fabricates a source/claim to complete a task.
- Comfortable escalating uncertainty.
- Can manage client dependencies without becoming passive.
- Process-minded but not bureaucratic.
- Learns tools quickly.

## Interview prompts
- Give an example of solving a problem when your manager was unavailable.
- Describe how you organise multiple client workflows and deadlines.
- Tell me about a time the written SOP was wrong or incomplete.
- How do you decide whether to ask, act or escalate?
- What kind of repetitive work are you unusually good at?
- What feedback changed how you work?

## Test
Give a messy mock client week: missing recording, conflicting source, late approval, editor revision, performance anomaly. Ask candidate to prioritise and document actions without inventing facts.
